false},"open_issues":3,"closed_issues":2535,"state":"closed","created_at":"2025-11-27T20:29:18Z","updated_at":"2026-10-20T18:39:31Z","due_on":null,"closed_at":"2026-06-19T16:54:35Z"},"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-02-19T23:38:20Z","updated_at":"2026-02-20T02:32:18Z","closed_at":"2026-02-20T02:31:49Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/116512","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116512","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116512.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116512.patch","merged_at":"2026-02-20T02:31:49Z"},"body":"- Follow-up to #112041\r\n- Follow-up to #116486\r\n\r\nNow that all the non-module tests are migrated to implementation files, it's now feasible to make slightly more involved changes:\r\n\r\n1. Only define `TESTS_ENABLED` where it's absolutely necessary. With slightly more generous forward-declares, the only remaining spots in the repo that use this define are implementation files in `main` and `modules/gdscript`. Previously we were passing this to *literally every source file*, which was a bit excessive\r\n\r\n2. Declare doctest config defines in `test_macros.h`. This is cleaner than trying to pass them as compilation arguments, as this file is acting as a wrapper for `doctest.h` already. As such, we don't need to declare these in individual `SCsub` files and hope that every module is perfectly synced with our main testing `SCsub`\r\n\r\n3. Created dedicated header/impl files for `SignalWatcher`; moved the relevant macros to that header.\r\n\r\n4. Moved the relevant `DisplayServerMock` macros to `display_server_mock.h`, and migrated even more functions to the implementation file.\r\n\r\n5. Slimmed down includes in `test_macros.h`, and consequently added the relevant includes to individual files when relevant. Made this an IWYU pass as well, with unnecessary includes being removed alongside an occasional `IWYU pragma:`.\r\n\r\n6. Fixed typo (`WEB_EMABLED` → `WEB_ENABLED`) 😅 ","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116512/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116512/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}